{
  "slug": "movies",
  "label": "Movies",
  "order": 2,
  "description": "Every Persona 5 Royal movie theater, its screening window, the social stat it raises and any special event it unlocks.",
  "source": {
    "href": "https://samurai-gamers.com/persona-5/movie-theater-guide/",
    "label": "Movie Theater Guide",
    "credit": "Wolf Knight"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The movies are a reliable way to turn one afternoon or evening into social stat points, and a first viewing is worth more than a repeat. Each theater keeps its own schedule, so this guide lists what is showing where and when."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "You can watch movies in theaters found in Shibuya, Shinjuki, and Yongen-Jaya to increase your social stats. The theaters are open during the day, after school, and in the evening."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Seeing a movie for the first time grants you +3 in a specific social stat. Meanwhile, watching a movie you have already seen only grants a +1 increase. An exception to this is when watching a movie during special events with one of your friends. Doing grants you the normal +3 increase in a social stat, regardless of having watched it before or not."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Similar to DVDs, after reading the book Cinema Treasures, the social stat increases gained is raised by one point."
    },
